  "details": {
   "type": "monstrosity (titan)",
   "size": "gargantuan",
   "alignment": "",
   "xp": "",
   "numberAppearing": "1",
   "resistances": "",
   "immunities": "fire, poison, non-magical, condition:charmed, condition:frightened, condition:paralysed, condition:poisoned",
   "vulnerabilities": "",
   "senses": "Blindsight 120ft",
   "isSolo": true,
   "levelText": "Mythic",
   "page": 0,
   "description": "<p><em>Gargantuan monstrosity (titan)</em></p><p><strong>GM:</strong> The world's last argument. It wakes once in a generation and walks until something stops it or it is sated. With Tiamat and Bahamut, the only creatures in this book beyond the 24th-level scale.</p><p><strong>Solo:</strong> acts twice a round, on its initiative and again 10 lower (the system adds its second turn; the second repeats its attacks, never a spell or limited ability). Anything that stops it acting, attacking, moving or casting ends after two of its turns (one, the second time in a fight), then nothing of the kind affects it until the end of the following round; the first time it drops to half HP every condition and hostile effect ends and its breath weapons and other limited-use abilities recover (not its spells); area, aura and ongoing damage and regeneration come once a round, at the start of its first turn (all automatic). An effect that would kill it outright, banish or imprison it, or Exhaustion from a spell, costs it its next two turns instead (yours to run); only one of Harm and Mass Harm can affect it in a fight. Damage to 0 HP still kills it.</p>",
   "treasure": "<p>Treasure type <strong>N</strong> (see the Treasure tables).</p>"
  }
 },
